\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 ANTIHUNTER DIGI NODE\

\fs36 TIER 3 \'96 POPULATED PCB
\f1\b0\fs30 \cf0 \
\
A fully assembled PCB, soldered and bench-tested, on its factory antennas. Meshtastic is flashed on the radio with the serial link to the node already configured.\
\
\

\f0\b IN THE BOX
\f1\b0 \
\
Populated 82 mm PCB, 16 GB microSD fitted\
Factory U.FL antennas: flat 2.4 GHz film, coiled LoRa whip, ceramic GPS patch\
\
You supply: power over USB or your own regulated 5 V, and a housing if you want one.\
\
\

\f0\b SET IT UP
\f1\b0 \
\
1. Fit the three U.FL antennas. Hold each connector parallel to the board, align the rims, press straight down until it clicks. Do not press at an angle. A crushed socket means a new module.\
\
GPS antenna to the GPS module, long black to the LoRa radio, film antenna that says 2.4GHz to the XIAO ESP32-S3.\
\
2. Never power the node with the LoRa antenna missing.\
\
3. Flash AntiHunter on the ESP32 over USB. Web flasher: lukeswitz.github.io/AntiHunter. Pick Full for the web UI, or Headless for quiet field ops.\
\
4. Set the LoRa region on the radio. It ships UNSET, which means receive only, and the node will not answer over mesh until you set it.\
\
5. Change the Bluetooth pairing pin on the radio. Every unit ships with the same one.\
\
6. Make your own encrypted Meshtastic channel primary and turn the public default channel off.\
\
7. Full firmware: join the 
\f0\b Antihunter
\f1\b0  WiFi AP, password 
\f0\b antihunt3r123
\f1\b0 , open http://192.168.4.1 and change those credentials first.\
\
\

\f0\b POWER
\f1\b0 \
\
Regulated 5 V only, from USB, a bench supply set to 5 V, a proper DC-DC regulator or a UPS board. Never wire 18650 cells or an unregulated supply to the PCB. Under 4.5 V it runs unstable. One USB cable at a time: the ESP32 and the radio share the power rails.\
\
\

